===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lbl|en|intransitive}} To [[lie]] in a hammock.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1901|author=w:Yone Noguchi|title=[https://books.google.com/books?id=QPMJAwAAQBAJ&pg=PA113&dq=hammocked&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CEAQ6AEwAzgoahUKEwjUrpHe-JfIAhUEMogKHZyvAzU#v=onepage&q=hammocked&f=false The American Diary of a Japanese Girl] {{w|The American Diary of a Japanese Girl|(wiki article)}}|passage="I fancied that we — I and who? — '''hammocked''' among the summer breezes."}}
# {{lbl|en|transitive|of a cloth}} To hang in a way that resembles a hammock.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=w:Mary Jo Putney; Patricia Rice; {{w|Susan King (novelist)|Susan King}}|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=WTKhAQAAQBAJ&pg=PT30&dq=%22she+hammocked%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CC0Q6AEwA2oVChMI77C9n-KXyAIVASmICh2qLgHn#v=onepage&q=%22she%20hammocked%22&f=false|title=Christmas Roses: Love Blooms in Winter
|passage="She '''hammocked''' their plaids between the table and the bed, then edged her way past Kenneth as she approached the central hearth."}}
# {{lbl|en|transitive}} To make something be wrapped tight, like in a hammock.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1960|author=w:John D. MacDonald|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=uR7IAwAAQBAJ&pg=PT115&dq=%22she+hammocked%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CCEQ6AEwAWoVChMIhNf1r_KXyAIVCZSICh2Biwzo#v=onepage&q=%22she%20hammocked%22&f=false|title=The Only Girl in the Game
|passage="She '''hammocked''' her breasts into her bra, snapped it, hitched at it, and gave herself a profile glance in the mirror."}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|broadcasting}} To [[schedule]] (a new or unpopular [[programme]]) between two popular ones in the hope that viewers will watch it.
#: {{cot|en|tentpole}}

